<Folder><name>10-14 · Nihonbashi arrive</name>
<Placemark>
        <name>1. Hotel LiVEMAX</name>
        <styleUrl>#style-d1-arrival</styleUrl>
        <description>Hours: check-in 15:00
Stay 1h 30m
End of this walk.
</description>
        <Point><coordinates>139.780836,35.68258,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>10-15 · Asakusa · Kappabashi · Ueno</name>
<Placemark>
        <name>1. Kaminarimon</name>
        <styleUrl>#style-d2-asakusa</styleUrl>
        <description>Stay 15 min
Then 2 min walk to next.
Giant red lantern gate. Photo, then walk through.</description>
        <Point><coordinates>139.79655,35.71107,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
<Placemark>
        <name>2. Nakamise</name>
        <styleUrl>#style-d2-asakusa</styleUrl>
        <description>Stay 20 min
Then 4 min walk to next.
Souvenir lane to the temple. Ningyo-yaki, senbei, cheap fans.</description>
        <Point><coordinates>139.79665,35.71215,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
<Placemark>
        <name>3. Sensō-ji</name>
        <styleUrl>#style-d2-asakusa</styleUrl>
        <description>Hours: hall 06:00–17:00
Stay 35 min
Then 4 min walk to next.
Tokyo’s oldest temple. Incense, main hall, pagoda.</description>
        <Point><coordinates>139.79666,35.71477,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
<Placemark>
        <name>4. Shin-Nakamise</name>
        <styleUrl>#style-d2-asakusa</styleUrl>
        <description>Hours: ~10:00–20:00
Stay 15 min
Then 8 min walk to next.
Covered shopping arcade beside Nakamise — not a second temple.</description>
        <Point><coordinates>139.7954,35.7128,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
<Placemark>
        <name>5. Asakusa Menchi</name>
        <styleUrl>#style-d2-asakusa</styleUrl>
        <description>Hours: ~10:00–18:00
Stay 25 min
Then 10 min walk to next.
Menchi-katsu at Kaminarimon. The Asakusa lunch. Opens around 10:00.</description>
        <Point><coordinates>139.7964,35.71085,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
<Placemark>
        <name>6. Kappabashi</name>
        <styleUrl>#style-d2-asakusa</styleUrl>
        <description>Hours: 10:00–17:00
Stay 40 min
Then 18 min walk to next.
Chef-supply street: knives, plastic food, ceramics.</description>
        <Point><coordinates>139.7886,35.7139,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
<Placemark>
        <name>7. Ameyoko</name>
        <styleUrl>#style-d2-asakusa</styleUrl>
        <description>Hours: ~10:00–19:00
Stay 40 min
Then 8 min walk to next.
Open-air market under the JR tracks. Lunch window here.</description>
        <Point><coordinates>139.7745,35.7095,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
<Placemark>
        <name>8. Ueno Park</name>
        <styleUrl>#style-d2-asakusa</styleUrl>
        <description>Stay 40 min
End of this walk.
Park + pond next to Ameyoko. Sit, don’t museum-sprint.</description>
        <Point><coordinates>139.7717,35.7148,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
<Placemark>
        <name>Route · Asakusa · Kappabashi · Ueno</name>
        <styleUrl>#style-d2-asakusa</styleUrl>
        <LineString>
          <tessellate>1</tessellate>
          <coordinates>139.79655,35.71107,0 139.79665,35.71215,0 139.79666,35.71477,0 139.7954,35.7128,0 139.7964,35.71085,0 139.7886,35.7139,0 139.7745,35.7095,0 139.7717,35.7148,0</coordinates>
        </LineString>
      </Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>10-15 · Shinjuku sunset</name>
<Placemark>
        <name>1. Shinjuku Gyoen (optional)</name>
        <styleUrl>#style-d2-shinjuku</styleUrl>
        <description>Hours: 09:00–16:30 last 16:00
Stay 40 min
Then 15 min walk to next.
Drop if Ueno ran long. Deck matters more.</description>
